<p class="text-base md:text-lg leading-relaxed text-on-primary-container m-0">A broken jaw (mandibular fracture) is a facial bone fracture of the lower or upper jaw. The most reliable broken jaw symptoms are severe jaw pain, rapid facial swelling, a sudden change in how the teeth meet (malocclusion), and numbness of the lower lip, chin, or tongue after facial trauma. Urgent maxillofacial care is required within 24–72 hours for the best outcome.</p>
